s settled into a convention yet  because it doesn't seem to have settled  at all but it's there it is a real thing  Cory last thing before we let you go  what's sort of like the biggest  controversy you've been involved in at  merriam-webster like what counts as a  major upheaval or controversy in the  dictionary  world I think the answer to that would  have to be when merriam-webster entered  a second meaning of the word marriage  that covered same-sex marriage this off  back in this is back in 2003 and which  is actually kind of late but it bucked  against the idea of the dictionary being  an authority of the dictionary setting  boundaries and so it was about a solid  month of at that point I was hint I was  the managing editor for correspondence  and that it was a solid month of just  answering people's very angry emails  about how can you do this you are read  you are literally redefining marriage  the courts will look to the dictionaries  to determine what marriage is well  what's interesting about that Cory is in  2003 is when our home state of  Massachusetts  I believe legalize same-sex marriage so  if you're thinking of merriam-webster as  an American dictionary there were at  that point places in America where  marriage did include same-sex marriages  absolutely and even if there hadn't been  even if same-sex marriage had continued  to be illegal across states and illegal  federally that doesn't matter we enter a  lot of work for illegal acts in the  dictionary I mean me and her murder but  we're not advocating that people go out  and murder people so but it was this  very interesting sort of you know the  dictionary mirroring what was already  happening in the culture and people  responding as if the dictionary was  leading the culture as opposed to  reflecting it that's probably the  biggest controversy I've been a part of  well the book is fascinating it's called  word by word it's in bookstores and  we've been speaking with the book's  author Corey Stamper Corey thanks so  much for talking to us about this thanks  for having me this is great

